<Project>
  <!--
    Repo-wide NuGet version overrides to patch transitive dependency CVEs.

    Scriban: 7.2.5, WITH ABP's OWN SCRIBAN ENGINE BYPASSED.
    Volo.Abp.TextTemplating.Scriban 10.0.2 is compiled against Scriban 6.x (its nuspec asks
    for 6.3.0), where Scriban.Parsing.ParserOptions is a different kind of type than in 7.x.
    ABP's ScribanTemplateRenderingEngine therefore throws, the moment its Template.Parse
    call is JIT-compiled against Scriban 7,
        System.TypeLoadException: Could not load type 'Scriban.Parsing.ParserOptions'
        from assembly 'Volo.Abp.TextTemplating.Scriban' due to value type mismatch
    i.e. EVERY ABP text template fails to render: the forgot-password reset email, the
    email-confirmation mail, etc. The account pages return 500 and no mail is ever sent.
    Build + unit tests of the old setup do NOT catch this (same trap as the AutoMapper
    note below); only an actual template render does — verified 2026-08-26 by POSTing
    /Account/ForgotPassword: 7.2.2 -> TypeLoadException, 6.6.0 -> 302 + mail rendered.

    The fix: Apya.Platform.TextTemplating.ApyaScribanTemplateRenderingEngine (Domain) is the
    same engine compiled against Scriban 7, and PlatformDomainModule points
    AbpTextTemplatingOptions.RenderingEngines["Scriban"] at it. AbpTemplateRenderer resolves
    the engine by that registered type, so ABP's own engine is never instantiated and never
    JIT-compiled. ApyaScribanTemplateRenderingEngine_Tests (EntityFrameworkCore.Tests) guards
    this — keep it green whenever Scriban or ABP is bumped. Control run 2026-10-30: ABP's own
    engine DOES throw System.TypeLoadException with Scriban 7.2.5 in the test host.
    This closes all 12 advisories that 6.6.0 carried (GHSA-5wr9-m6jw-xx44 critical, 7 high,
    4 medium). 7.5.3 was also advisory-free when checked (2026-10-30); 7.2.5 is what
    ABP 10.6/10.7 itself ships and is tested against.

    Where Scriban 7 starts in ABP, per the nuspecs of Volo.Abp.TextTemplating.Scriban:
    10.0.x/10.1.x -> 6.3.0, 10.2.x/10.3.0 -> 7.0.0, 10.4/10.5 -> 7.2.1, 10.6/10.7 -> 7.2.5.
    (An earlier note here said 10.4; the first Scriban-7 build is 10.2.0.) Once ABP is
    upgraded to >= 10.2, delete the engine class and the RenderingEngines override.

    AutoMapper: Volo.Abp.AutoMapper 10.0.2 ships AutoMapper 14.0.0 (GHSA-rvv3-g6hj-g44x / CVE-2026-32933).
    DO NOT bump to 15.x: AutoMapper 15 changed the MapperConfiguration ctor
    (removed MapperConfiguration(MapperConfigurationExpression)), which ABP 10.0.2
    calls — causing MissingMethodException at runtime container resolution so EVERY
    AutoMapper-backed /api/app/* returns 500. Build + unit tests do NOT catch this;
    only a live authenticated API call does (verified 2026-06-08 on main a845805).
    Stay on 14.0.0 until ABP is upgraded to a build compiled against AutoMapper 15.x.
    Trade-off: CVE-2026-32933 stays open in dev (no 14.x fix exists).

  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Scriban" Version="7.2.5" />
    <PackageReference Include="AutoMapper" Version="14.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
